Source: pg-parquet
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~), cargo, cmake, pkg-config, libssl-dev,
 clang | clang-21 | clang-20 | clang-19 | clang-18 | clang-17 | clang-16,
 libclang-dev | libclang-21-dev | libclang-20-dev | libclang-19-dev | libclang-18-dev | libclang-17-dev | libclang-16-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/CrunchyData/pg_parquet

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-parquet
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-pg-parquet
Depends: postgresql-PGVERSION, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Copy to/from Parquet in S3 from within PostgreSQL
  pg_parquet is a PostgreSQL extension that allows you to read and write Parquet files,
  which are located in S3 or file system, from PostgreSQL via COPY TO/FROM commands.
  It depends on Apache Arrow project to read and write Parquet files and pgrx project to extend PostgreSQL's COPY command.


